\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-90\li90\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord of all being, throned afar,
\par Thy glory flames from sun and star;
\par Centre and soul of every sphere, 
\par Yet to each loving heart how near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sun of our life, thy quickening ray
\par Sheds on our path the glow of day;
\par Star of our hope, Thy softened light
\par Cheers the long watches of the night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Our midnight is Thy smile withdrawn,
\par Our noontide is Thy gracious dawn,
\par Our rainbow arch, Thy mercy's sign;
\par All, save the clouds of sin, are Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord of all life, below, above,
\par Whose light is truth, whose warmth is love,
\par Before Thy ever-blazing throne
\par We ask no lustre of our own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Grant us Thy truth to make us free,
\par And kindling hearts that burn for Thee,
\par Till all Thy living altars claim
\par One holy light, one heavenly flame.
\par                                          Amen.
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f1\fs16 
\par 
\par }

